description:
Two matchStrings, unioned (default matchStringsStrategy `any`), BOTH tolerating any number of comment-only lines between the annotation and the pin (`(?:\s*#[^
]*
)*`) — the first covers a scalar value (`key: value`), the second a YAML list item (`- "pkg==version"`), the shape a `_pip_packages:`-style list uses, which the earlier scalar-only pattern never matched. The scalar pattern originally tolerated only whitespace (`\s+`) between the annotation and the key, not an intervening `#` comment line — `[^
]*` stops at the newline and `\s+` cannot cross a comment line's leading `#`, so an annotation followed by even one explanatory comment before the pin silently produced NO match: the checker (which tracks annotation state across comment lines by design) accepted it, but Renovate itself never tracked it. That gap is exactly the failure mode this PR exists to close, so the scalar pattern now mirrors the list-item pattern's comment-skipping gap.
